				1733,
				4
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Revert to standard binary names after Electron profile testing\n\nRestore Cargo.toml and tauri.conf.json to their standard configuration by removing the verbose Electron profile build configuration descriptors. The binary, library, package name, and product identifiers all revert from the long debug-specific format back to plain \"Mountain\".\n\nClean up the resource mapping in tauri.conf.json by reorganizing the Sky target entries and removing duplicate paths. Delete the backup files (Cargo.toml.Backup and tauri.conf.json.Backup) that were created during the testing phase.\n\nReset the application identifier to the standard \"fiddee.editor.binary\" and remove the Electron-specific suffixes. All configuration now points to the canonical build artifacts.",
			"SHA": "c9bbf1212e6a2309f2a8ccc2ec91edb9a183a75b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T17:54:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1735,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Configure debug build artifacts for Electron profile testing\n\nRename the Mountain binary and package identifiers to include the full build configuration descriptor: DevelopmentNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Debug_ElectronProfile_EsbuildCompiler_Mountain. This distinguishes the debug build targeting the Electron runtime environment from production builds.\n\nUpdate tauri.conf.json resources to explicitly map all Sky build targets (Browser, Electron, Bundled, BrowserProxy, Isolation, Favicon, Manifest.json, Mountain, Worker.js, and Static/* assets) for bundling. Reorganize the resource array to group related entries and remove redundant paths.\n\nAlso remove the now-unused WorkspaceFileService module declaration from Source/Workspace/mod.rs, keeping only the documentation summary for workspace lifecycle handling.\n\nThis configuration enables testing the MetroHastings integration against the Electron profile while preserving backup copies of the original Cargo.toml and tauri.conf.json.",
			"SHA": "c62faa2f412251a2fbfae0e170e8b81fe5123ab4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T17:31:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1733,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove dead IPC and internal modules\n\nEliminate unused submodules from the ApplicationState, IPC, and ProcessManagement layers: dead `PathResolution`, `Recovery`, `Serialization` in Internal; `Message`, `Connection`, `Encryption`, `Security`, `WindAirCommands`, `WindServiceAdapters`, and `Permission` in IPC; plus `WorkspaceContainsGlob` in ProcessManagement.\n\nCondense module documentation to focused summaries, removing migration roadmaps and legacy notes. Preserve only actively-used modules (`ExtensionScanner`, `Persistence`, `TextProcessing`, `Common`, `TauriIPCServer_Old`, `AdvancedFeatures`, `ConfigurationBridge`, `StatusReporter`, `WindAdvancedSync`, `DevLog`, `SkyEmit`, `EmitWithTraceparent`, `UriComponents`, `WindServiceHandlers`, and `NodeResolver`).\n\nThis cleanup reduces noise in the module tree and ensures only live code paths remain in scope.",
			"SHA": "68fa97ee5585b514125db6b618b5c6ea7ec4f243"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
